# BEHIND THE YES OF `$isPrototypeChainPlain` THE LIBRARY's OWN TEXT LEAVES LOOKS OUT AT A BIRTH. The yes reads bytes that the run time keeps; no record of the walk stands there for a net to ask.
# Under testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime the yes is held to the objects themselves, for each class asked: the own `prototype` of the class object, read without making it, and each link above it, walked in step with the records of the
# classes, the tables that arm the bytes: each is the prototype object that the record's class has, and the last stands below Object.prototype. What lies ON those objects is not asked.
# RUN(FORM): walk f4 mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime
# FORM: [[yes]]: boolean @Boolean = AreMembersUnchanged
# FORM: AskObjectAgain {{*}}, -, [[yes]] key="prototype" function=f2 [asksChainAbovePrototype]
# FORM: AskObjectAgain {{*}}, -, [[yes]] key="prototype" function=f3 [asksChainAbovePrototype]
# Nothing touched, and what the promise allows: no stop.
# RUN(QUIET): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function () { };
# QUIET: yes yes
# QUIET-NEXT: yes yes
# QUIET-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(STORED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base) { Meter.prototype.other = function () { }; Base.prototype.more = 1; Base.prototype.reach = function () { return "wrapped"; }; };
# STORED: yes yes
# STORED-NEXT: yes yes
# STORED-NEXT: exited with 0
# A link that changes ends the yes, and the net is not asked.
# RUN(LINK): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base) { Object.setPrototypeOf(Meter.prototype, { }); };
# LINK: yes yes
# LINK-NEXT: no no
# LINK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(ABOVE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base) { Object.setPrototypeOf(Base.prototype, { }); };
# ABOVE: yes yes
# ABOVE-NEXT: no no
# ABOVE-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(REPLACED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base, Other) { Other.prototype = { }; };
# REPLACED: yes yes
# REPLACED-NEXT: no no
# REPLACED-NEXT: exited with 0
# The lie, testing=GuardsAndFactsAreTakenToHold: the question is answered yes while the program is compiled; the guards still begin in front of it. On an untouched program the net stays silent under it.
# RUN(LIEQUIET): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime,GuardsAndFactsAreTakenToHold keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function () { };
# LIEQUIET: yes yes
# LIEQUIET-NEXT: yes yes
# LIEQUIET-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(LIELINK): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime,GuardsAndFactsAreTakenToHold keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base) { Object.setPrototypeOf(Meter.prototype, { }); };
# LIELINK: yes yes
# LIELINK-NEXT: AOT: the yes to the question whether the chain above the prototype of a class is plain promises that no link above the prototype of the class has changed, and the objects, walked in step with the records of the classes, are others.
# LIELINK: crashed with
# RUN(LIEABOVE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime,GuardsAndFactsAreTakenToHold keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base) { Object.setPrototypeOf(Base.prototype, { }); };
# LIEABOVE: yes yes
# LIEABOVE-NEXT: AOT: the yes to the question whether the chain above the prototype of a class is plain promises that no link above the prototype of the class has changed
# LIEABOVE: crashed with
# Every object on the chain is still a holder that the tables know, and one is passed over: a walk that asked only "is this a known holder" would pass it.
# RUN(LIESKIPS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime,GuardsAndFactsAreTakenToHold keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base) { Object.setPrototypeOf(Meter.prototype, Object.prototype); };
# LIESKIPS: yes yes
# LIESKIPS-NEXT: AOT: the yes to the question whether the chain above the prototype of a class is plain promises that no link above the prototype of the class has changed
